########## #251
Security: torch<2.5 constraint in 2.0.0 forces use of vulnerable torch versions. | state=open | created=2026-02-23 | updated=2026-02-23 | comments=0
## Problem

⁠ uni2ts==2.0.0 ⁠ requires ⁠ torch>=2.1,<2.5 ⁠, which prevents upgrading to
torch 2.5+ and forces production environments to pin torch to versions
currently flagged with active CVEs by security scanners.

This creates a hard blocker: upgrading ⁠ uni2ts ⁠ to fix its own
vulnerability requires pinning ⁠ torch ⁠ to a version range with known
security issues.

## Relation to existing work

This is related to PR #216 (relax dependencies) and issue #133
(test failure with torch 2.5). We understand the ⁠ <2.5 ⁠ upper bound
was introduced due to a test regression in ⁠ test_attention.py ⁠, but
from a security standpoint this constraint is now actively harmful
for production users.

## Our environment

•⁠  ⁠⁠ uni2ts ⁠: trying to upgrade from ⁠ 1.x ⁠ → ⁠ 2.0.0 ⁠
•⁠  ⁠⁠ torch ⁠: currently on ⁠ ^2.5.1 ⁠ (not vulnerable)
•⁠  ⁠Upgrading to ⁠ uni2ts==2.0.0 ⁠ forces torch to ⁠ <2.5 ⁠ (vulnerable)

## Request

Could you prioritize merging PR #216 or releasing a patch that relaxes
the ⁠ torch ⁠ upper bound? Even making ⁠ torch>=2.5 ⁠ work — perhaps with
the attention fix from issue #133 — would unblock us.

We're happy to help test a candidate fix against torch 2.5+.
